# Deliberate, justified exceptions to Trivy's Kubernetes misconfiguration
# checks -- each entry below is a real, necessary requirement for what that
# specific workload does, not an oversight. IDs and path-scoping verified by
# running `trivy config` locally against the exact file before adding.
# See docs/AUDIT.md (SEC-012) for the broader hardening pass that addresses
# everything else Trivy flags across the rest of the repo.

# sysctl-fix DaemonSet: applies host-level sysctls (disabling ICMP redirects)
# to every k3s node. Genuinely requires hostNetwork, hostPID, and privileged --
# there is no less-privileged way to reach the host's sysctl namespace from
# inside a container.
KSV-0009 path:kubernetes/system/infrastructure/sysctl-fix.yml
KSV-0010 path:kubernetes/system/infrastructure/sysctl-fix.yml
KSV-0017 path:kubernetes/system/infrastructure/sysctl-fix.yml
KSV-0118 path:kubernetes/system/infrastructure/sysctl-fix.yml

# SABnzbd's Mullvad WireGuard kill-switch init container: NET_ADMIN is needed
# to create the wg0 interface and manage iptables; SYS_MODULE is needed to
# load the wireguard kernel module. This whole stack is moving to a dedicated
# LXC (WRK-006) where this same requirement applies at the LXC level instead --
# the manifest here stays live until that cutover completes.
KSV-0022 path:kubernetes/apps/jellyfin/usenet.yml
KSV-0120 path:kubernetes/apps/jellyfin/usenet.yml

# sysctl-fix DaemonSet's container is privileged: true -- allowPrivilegeEscalation
# is moot there (privileged mode already implies it), and the blast radius of
# testing a contradictory combination on a DaemonSet running on every node wasn't
# worth it for a no-op setting.
KSV-0001 path:kubernetes/system/infrastructure/sysctl-fix.yml

# False positives: Trivy pattern-matches ConfigMap key/value names like "key" or
# "client_secret" without understanding what they actually contain. Verified each
# one directly:
#   - authelia-config: client_secret values are argon2id *hashes* (the actual
#     plaintext secret lives with each OIDC client, e.g. Grafana -- Authelia only
#     stores the hash to verify it); jwt_secret/session secret/encryption_key/
#     hmac_secret/oidc-issuer-private-key are all Vault Agent template refs
#     ({{ secret "/config/secrets/X" }}), resolved at runtime, not literal values.
#   - headscale-config: only contains file *paths* to private keys, not the keys
#     themselves; client_secret is injected via env var from a real Secret object,
#     never stored in this ConfigMap at all.
#   - homepage-config: all {{HOMEPAGE_VAR_*}} placeholders, resolved via
#     envFrom: secretRef: homepage-secrets at runtime.
KSV-01010 path:kubernetes/apps/authelia/configmap.yml
KSV-01010 path:kubernetes/apps/headscale/config.yml
KSV-01010 path:kubernetes/apps/homepage/homepage.yml

# 2026-08-16: garage/main.tf's aws_s3_bucket resources talk to Garage's own
# S3-compatible endpoint (see providers.tf), not real AWS -- these checks are for
# AWS-specific APIs/features Garage doesn't implement, not oversights:
#   - AWS-0086/0087/0091/0093 (S3 public-access-block): Garage doesn't implement
#     AWS's PutPublicAccessBlock API at all (it's outside Garage's documented S3
#     compatibility scope), so an aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block resource here
#     would fail to apply. Also moot in practice regardless -- these buckets are
#     ClusterIP-only (garage.apps.svc.cluster.local), never on any public-exposure
#     allowlist (see docs/EXPOSURE.md), so there is no public-internet path to
#     "accidentally public" in the first place.
#   - AWS-0132 (Customer Managed Keys / AWS KMS): Garage has no KMS integration:
#     setting kms_master_key_id would either be silently ignored or fail the apply.
AWS-0086 path:terraform/stacks/garage/main.tf
AWS-0087 path:terraform/stacks/garage/main.tf
AWS-0091 path:terraform/stacks/garage/main.tf
AWS-0093 path:terraform/stacks/garage/main.tf
AWS-0132 path:terraform/stacks/garage/main.tf

# vault-server Role: both grants are documented requirements of Vault's Kubernetes
# auth backend (service_registration.kubernetes is enabled; Vault 1.17.2 execs the
# SA token helper). IDs verified with trivy 0.75.0 against this exact file.
KSV-0053 path:kubernetes/system/vault/rbac.yml
KSV-0056 path:kubernetes/system/vault/rbac.yml

# KSV-0014 readOnlyRootFilesystem: each of these workloads writes to its own root
# filesystem at run time. Evidence and evidence classes: ADR-049.
# Applied and rolled back after breaking in production:
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/authelia/authelia.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/firefly/firefly.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/scanopy/scanopy.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/scrutiny/scrutiny.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/homepage/homepage.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/open-webui/open-webui.yml
# Writes to /usr or /usr/local/bin, provable from the script in the same file:
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/system/velero/restore-test.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/system/velero/r2-usage-guard.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/system/monitoring/dr-game-day.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/system/monitoring/tailnet-route-drift-check.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/system/monitoring/weekly-report.yml
# NOT proven incompatible -- untested open questions, still owed an attempt:
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/freshrss/deployment.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/crowdsec/crowdsec.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/onlyoffice/onlyoffice.yml
KSV-0014 path:kubernetes/apps/myspeed/myspeed.yml

# KSV-0119 NET_RAW: both are already privileged:true, so the capability is
# redundant. subnet-router needs that privilege to set src_valid_mark; scanopy
# needs raw sockets to scan. Details: ADR-049.
KSV-0119 path:kubernetes/apps/headscale/subnet-router.yml
KSV-0119 path:kubernetes/apps/scanopy/scanopy.yml

# KSV-0121 disallowed volume type: kube-bench exists to read the node's kubelet
# config, scrutiny-collector needs hostPID for host S.M.A.R.T. data. See ADR-049.
KSV-0121 path:kubernetes/apps/kube-bench/kube-bench.yml
KSV-0121 path:kubernetes/apps/scrutiny/scrutiny.yml

# KSV-0041 cluster-wide secret read: the operator must read every Secret to find
# image references inside them. Scoping it down stops it scanning those.
KSV-0041 path:kubernetes/apps/trivy-operator/trivy-operator.yml
